    description: "Topics — a tracker over #topic pieces: durable units of shared attention\n" +
      "(CT-1878). Deliberately minimal: no statuses, labels, or assignees; topics\n" +
      "sort by last activity. Replaces Linear / GitHub issues / loose process docs\n" +
      "for the team; PR workflows stay in GitHub and arrive here as links.\n" +
      "\n" +
      "Headless use: survey the whole board with one bounded read of `index` — a\n" +
      "row IS its topic, so a row's own address (`--select index[].@`) is what\n" +
      "that topic's reads and verbs take as the piece. File with `addTopic`,\n" +
      "title and optional initial body in one call, then work on the topic\n" +
      "directly: the body is its living document, the thread its append-only\n" +
      "deliberation. Sign every mutation with `agentName` — Fabric records the\n" +
